   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5b44cac50a894e589871012b",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21c1d174519bf2720dc4edf000a76668?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPW-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21c1d174519bf2720dc4edf000a76668?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21c1d174519bf2720dc4edf000a76668?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21c1d174519bf2720dc4edf000a76668?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Peter Winckles",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5b44cac50a894e589871012b",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "@Geoff Scholl: I was just thinking about this ticket, and I’m not sure if it makes sense to migrate RELS-EXT as an RDF container rather than as a binary.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "At UW-Madison, and my assumption is that this is true for you as well, RELS-EXT describes relationships for the Fedora 3 object. When the object is migrated to Fedora 6 it loses the distinction between an object and its datastreams. Instead, objects are modeled as RDF containers that contain all of their datastreams, which are modeled as binaries.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Let’s look at a concrete example. We have object info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D in Fedora 3 which has the following RELS-EXT:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "attrs": {
         "language": "xml"
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "<rdf:RDF xmlns=\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/model#\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:fedora=\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/relations-external#\" xmlns:foxml=\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/foxml#\" xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\" xmlns:rdfs=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#\" xmlns:uwdc=\"https://digital.library.wisc.edu/1711.dl/rdf/1.0/relations#\" xmlns:uwdcr=\"https://digital.library.wisc.edu/1711.dl/vocabulary/resourcetype#\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" ID=\"RELS-EXT\">\r\n  <rdf:Description rdf:about=\"info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D\">\r\n    <hasModel rdf:resource=\"info:fedora/1711.dl:CModelUWDCObject\"></hasModel>\r\n    <hasModel rdf:resource=\"info:fedora/1711.dl:CModelMaster\"></hasModel>\r\n    <hasModel rdf:resource=\"info:fedora/1711.dl:CModelSimpleText\"></hasModel>\r\n    <fedora:isMemberOf rdf:resource=\"info:fedora/1711.dl:6YV6NVSHOUAN48A\"></fedora:isMemberOf>\r\n    <uwdc:isMemberOfProject rdf:resource=\"https://digital.library.wisc.edu/1711.dl/WWILibraryPrj\"></uwdc:isMemberOfProject>\r\n    <uwdc:hasAccessPolicy rdf:resource=\"https://digital.library.wisc.edu/1711.dl/Access-policy-open-access-all\"></uwdc:hasAccessPolicy>\r\n  </rdf:Description>\r\n</rdf:RDF>",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "codeBlock"
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Now, when that’s migrated to Fedora 6 there will be two resources, info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D, an RDF container, and info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D/RELS-EXT, a binary. If we changed the second to be a container, it becomes weird because those triples would be applied to info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D/RELS-EXT. That is to say, info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D/RELS-EXT is not a ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "type": "code"
           }
          ],
          "text": "info:fedora/1711.dl:CModelMaster",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " – info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D is.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "What might make sense instead is if RELS-EXT was not migrated at all and instead its triples were added to the container resource that represents the object.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Similarly, with RELS-INT, it might make sense to not migrate it at all and add its triples to the resources that they apply to.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
