     "updated": "2021-09-10T16:23:15.704-0300"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5db386745304a60c3a769d36",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Demian Katz",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5db386745304a60c3a769d36",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "5b44cac50a894e589871012b",
           "text": "@Peter Winckles"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": " , I agree – and I think the intent of our original ticket was actually exactly as you describe: that the triples from RELS-EXT be added to the container representing the original Fedora object, rather than as a binary XML datastream or a separate RDF container.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Depending on the possible complexities and confidence levels, I suppose it might be useful to have a configuration to choose either approach, or even both approaches – e.g. migrate the triples, but also keep the original document as a binary for historical purposes.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
