  "comment": {
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5b44cac50a894e589871012b",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21c1d174519bf2720dc4edf000a76668?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPW-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21c1d174519bf2720dc4edf000a76668?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21c1d174519bf2720dc4edf000a76668?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21c1d174519bf2720dc4edf000a76668?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Peter Winckles",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5b44cac50a894e589871012b",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>@Geoff Scholl: I was just thinking about this ticket, and I’m not sure if it makes sense to migrate RELS-EXT as an RDF container rather than as a binary.</p>\n\n<p>At UW-Madison, and my assumption is that this is true for you as well, RELS-EXT describes relationships for the Fedora 3 object. When the object is migrated to Fedora 6 it loses the distinction between an object and its datastreams. Instead, objects are modeled as RDF containers that contain all of their datastreams, which are modeled as binaries.</p>\n\n<p>Let’s look at a concrete example. We have object info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D in Fedora 3 which has the following RELS-EXT:</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-xml\"><span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;rdf:RDF xmlns=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/model#\"</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">xmlns:dc</span>=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\"</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">xmlns:fedora</span>=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/relations-external#\"</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">xmlns:foxml</span>=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/foxml#\"</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">xmlns:oai_dc</span>=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\"</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">xmlns:rdf</span>=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\"</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">xmlns:rdfs</span>=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#\"</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">xmlns:uwdc</span>=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"https://digital.library.wisc.edu/1711.dl/rdf/1.0/relations#\"</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">xmlns:uwdcr</span>=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"https://digital.library.wisc.edu/1711.dl/vocabulary/resourcetype#\"</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">xmlns:xsi</span>=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"</span> ID=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"RELS-EXT\"</span>&gt;</span>\r\n  <span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;rdf:Description rdf:about=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D\"</span>&gt;</span>\r\n    <span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;hasModel rdf:resource=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"info:fedora/1711.dl:CModelUWDCObject\"</span>&gt;</span><span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;/hasModel&gt;</span>\r\n    <span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;hasModel rdf:resource=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"info:fedora/1711.dl:CModelMaster\"</span>&gt;</span><span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;/hasModel&gt;</span>\r\n    <span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;hasModel rdf:resource=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"info:fedora/1711.dl:CModelSimpleText\"</span>&gt;</span><span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;/hasModel&gt;</span>\r\n    <span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;fedora:isMemberOf rdf:resource=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"info:fedora/1711.dl:6YV6NVSHOUAN48A\"</span>&gt;</span><span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;/fedora:isMemberOf&gt;</span>\r\n    <span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;uwdc:isMemberOfProject rdf:resource=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"https://digital.library.wisc.edu/1711.dl/WWILibraryPrj\"</span>&gt;</span><span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;/uwdc:isMemberOfProject&gt;</span>\r\n    <span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;uwdc:hasAccessPolicy rdf:resource=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"https://digital.library.wisc.edu/1711.dl/Access-policy-open-access-all\"</span>&gt;</span><span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;/uwdc:hasAccessPolicy&gt;</span>\r\n  <span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;/rdf:Description&gt;</span>\r\n<span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;/rdf:RDF&gt;</span></pre>\n</div></div>\n\n\n\n<p>Now, when that’s migrated to Fedora 6 there will be two resources, info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D, an RDF container, and info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D/RELS-EXT, a binary. If we changed the second to be a container, it becomes weird because those triples would be applied to info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D/RELS-EXT. That is to say, info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D/RELS-EXT is not a <tt>info:fedora/1711.dl:CModelMaster</tt> – info:fedora/1711.dl:52O74PJ27SFY58D is.</p>\n\n<p>What might make sense instead is if RELS-EXT was not migrated at all and instead its triples were added to the container resource that represents the object.</p>\n\n<p>Similarly, with RELS-INT, it might make sense to not migrate it at all and add its triples to the resources that they apply to.</p>",
     "created": "10/Sep/21 4:23 PM",
